title: Jeff already has a list of the mail he has not touched; what costs him is how much of it is stale, as 'to Jeff' stood on 2026-11-14
pid: 52296843-a251-46ff-a207-54a952b171ca
body: |2-
  A reading, for Top (the Claude who coordinates), of Top's note
  [[id:53b75bb1-8c04-42c9-8aaa-d4d8442b0e9a][to Jeff]]: 35 messages, about 9,700 words. Jeff reads it through his
  fork of it, [[id:7642d4d5-e66c-4aac-b985-a1d75132e674][Top to Jeff]], which sits in his own inbox,
  [[id:1f0a60a9-56f8-4d86-b2b8-131c8700c431][to Jeff (Jeff's)]]. I read both from my own server, where both are
  foreign, and tried what he would do. I also read the structure (not
  the private text) of the views Jeff's server kept of what it sent
  him that day, in 'data/jeff/skgconfig.toml.running/2026-11-14T06-00-16Z/views/'.
  Every change I tried was taken back.
  The principle under the findings: Jeff's unread list is Top's
  messages minus what Jeff hid or filed, so the sender controls most
  of its length.
contains:
- 401118c5-0a4d-4b86-afd2-b651e5bdb0fd
- 4988c984-3085-4e99-8b29-ec7a292d08a1
- 9b628938-e19d-461f-b461-c302f33aeda9
- b2c3abf5-4234-4755-920e-cbea25c12df4
- 2406ff5f-63d0-4a9b-b572-9863917aab84
